        "file": "block/vmdk.c",
        "start_line": 876,
        "end_line": 877,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Grain marker lba/size written in host endianness",
        "explanation": "The on-disk VMDK grain marker is little-endian, and the new read path decodes it with le32_to_cpu(marker->size). The write path stores data->lba and data->size without conversion. On big-endian hosts the written markers are byte-swapped, so the resulting streamOptimized images are corrupt and can't be read back, either by QEMU or by other tools.",
        "suggestion": "data->lba = cpu_to_le64(sector_num); data->size = cpu_to_le32(buf_len);",
        "evidence": "        data->size = buf_len;",
        "confidence": 0.85,
        "id": "58aff6974b54",
        "hunk_id": "block/vmdk.c#2",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "block/vmdk.c",
        "start_line": 932,
        "end_line": 941,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "security",
        "title": "Marker size check ignores header offset, allowing heap over-read",
        "explanation": "With markers, compressed_data = marker->data, which starts sizeof(VmdkGrainMarker) (12) bytes into cluster_buf. The bound check only enforces data_len <= buf_bytes. A crafted image with marker->size close to buf_bytes makes uncompress() read up to 12 bytes past the end of the heap buffer cluster_buf.",
        "suggestion": "When has_marker is set, check data_len > buf_bytes - sizeof(VmdkGrainMarker) (or compute the bound from compressed_data - cluster_buf).",
        "evidence": "    if (!data_len || data_len > buf_bytes) {",
        "confidence": 0.8,
        "id": "3f960a62e848",
        "hunk_id": "block/vmdk.c#4",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "block/vmdk.c",
        "start_line": 871,
        "end_line": 882,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "data-loss",
        "title": "Compressed grain written at offset_in_cluster but read from cluster start",
        "explanation": "When the write doesn't start at a cluster boundary, the marker and compressed data are written at cluster_offset + offset_in_cluster. Only nb_sectors are compressed, and lba is set to the unaligned sector_num. vmdk_read_extent always parses the marker at cluster_offset and expects a full decompressed cluster. It then reads garbage or returns -EINVAL when offset_in_cluster + n*512 > buf_len. Data from partial-cluster writes to a streamOptimized extent is therefore lost.",
        "suggestion": "Reject compressed writes that don't cover a whole cluster (offset_in_cluster != 0 or nb_sectors != cluster_sectors). Otherwise, build a full cluster buffer and write the marker at cluster_offset with lba set to the cluster's first sector.",
        "evidence": "                        cluster_offset + offset_in_cluster,",
        "confidence": 0.6,
        "id": "86f3be6fa3a3",
        "hunk_id": "block/vmdk.c#2",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "block/vmdk.c",
        "start_line": 923,
        "end_line": 928,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "error-handling",
        "title": "Short read of compressed grain treated as success",
        "explanation": "Only ret < 0 is treated as failure. A short read, such as a grain near EOF, leaves the rest of the g_malloc'd cluster_buf uninitialized, and those bytes are passed to uncompress() as compressed input. The result is nondeterministic decoding of uninitialized heap memory instead of a clean error.",
        "suggestion": "Use g_malloc0 for cluster_buf, or limit data_len to the number of bytes actually read (ret).",
        "evidence": "    if (ret < 0) {",
